TrustTunnel VPN endpoint daemon.

A modern open-source VPN server developed by AdGuard. By design,
TrustTunnel traffic is indistinguishable from regular HTTPS, allowing
it to bypass throttling and deep-packet inspection while maintaining
strong privacy protections.

This port builds the server-side binaries: `trusttunnel_endpoint`
(daemon listening on TLS/QUIC) and `trusttunnel_setup_wizard`
(interactive config generator with built-in ACME support).

The companion `security/trusttunnel-client` port provides the
client-side CLI binary.

WWW: https://github.com/TrustTunnel/TrustTunnel
